shizue-plot plays character cards as RisuAI and PocketRisu play them, and much
of what it does is ported from their behaviour and their code. Both are free
software under the GNU General Public License, version 3:

  RisuAI, by kwaroran and its contributors
  https://github.com/kwaroran/RisuAI
    The character card formats it reads (V1 to V3, charx, RisuRealm), the CBS
    macro language, lorebook activation, regex scripts, triggers and the Lua
    runtime with its API, HypaV3 memory, prompt presets and their parameters,
    and the request formats a model is called in (LLMFormat), with the
    instruct templates and transcripts its text formats write the chat in.

  PocketRisu, by its contributors
  https://github.com/PocketRisu/PocketRisu
    Model presets bound to each chat as a main and a sub model, the provider
    request adapters, the prompt templates written in their original words,
    and remote access from a phone through a tunnel, downloading cloudflared
    for it. The model registry's
    code — its types, snapshot resolution, catalog sync, profile updates and
    the request builder and adapters a preset on a profile runs through — is
    ported from PocketRisu's src/ts/preset (commit f71e1cc), and the tests hold
    the requests to a transcription of its adapters.

The model registry's data — the base providers and model profiles in
apps/plot/packages/llm/src/registry/bundled.json, taken from PocketRisu's
bundled copy at f71e1cc, and the catalog the app refreshes from — is the
PocketRisu Model Registry, dedicated to the public domain under CC0-1.0:

  PocketRisu Model Registry, by PocketRisu's contributors
  https://github.com/PocketRisu/pocketrisu-model-registry

Comments in the sources name the RisuAI or PocketRisu behaviour each part
follows. The published package also bundles third-party libraries and fonts,
each under its own license.

The app downloads the model its chat memory searches with on its first start,
from Hugging Face; it is not part of this program's code:

  KURE-v1, by the NLP & AI Lab at Korea University (nlpai-lab), under the MIT License
  https://huggingface.co/nlpai-lab/KURE-v1
    Downloaded as our int8 ONNX conversion of its weights,
    https://huggingface.co/rokrokss/KURE-v1-onnx, which keeps that license.

On a computer with neither Tailscale nor cloudflared, opening phone access
downloads Cloudflare's cloudflared, one pinned release from its GitHub
releases; it is not part of this program's code either:

  cloudflared, by Cloudflare, under the Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared
